1775:   // so iterating through every stream to find the ones that have a deferred reset is not a big
1776:   // deal. Furthermore, queueing a reset frame does not actually invoke the close stream callback.
1777:   // This is only done when the reset frame is sent. Thus, it's safe to work directly with the
1778:   // stream map.
1779:   // NOTE: The way we handle deferred reset is essentially best effort. If we intend to do a
1780:   //       deferred reset, we try to finish the stream, including writing any pending data frames.
1781:   //       If we cannot do this (potentially due to not enough window), we just reset the stream.
1782:   //       In general this behavior occurs only when we are trying to send immediate error messages
1783:   //       to short circuit requests. In the best effort case, we complete the stream before
1784:   //       resetting. In other cases, we just do the reset now which will blow away pending data
1785:   //       frames and release any memory associated with the stream.
